Fixes (all in harness/model-guide/, no test file touched):

- F1 (A3-1/C3-1) preview.sh: the input check runs into a temp staging
  folder first (`mktemp -d`, trap cleanup). A refused run writes nothing
  near the preview folder: an existing preview folder stays byte-identical,
  and no new folder stays behind, not even a parent that `mkdir -p` created.
  On success the script copies docs/, then the staged real-work.json wins
  over stale docs copies (the F13 order still holds).
- F2 (A3-2/C3-3) real-work.ts: the schema check now tests the type of each
  coverage key (`runs`, `first_run_date`, `last_run_date`,
  `share_known_route`, `share_with_result`, `paired_duplicates_left_out`)
  and of `generated_on`, before the run-sum check. A wrong type gives
  `input-check: schema`, exit 2, no traceback, no half-built preview.
- F3 (A3-3) preview.sh: a symlink inside an existing preview folder gives
  `preview: refused path <path>` (the path is the link), exit 2, one
  refusal line on stdout, no docs write. The line is stated in the header.
- F4 (C3-2/A3-4) preview.sh: the nav insert adds only the links that are
  missing, so a second preview over a published index keeps exactly one of
  each link.
- F5 (B2-1) publish.ts: the docs walk catches a stat failure (dangling
  symlink) and the hash read catches a read failure (unreadable file); each
  maps to `publish: drift <path>`, exit 2, no stack trace. preview.sh maps
  the same dangling-entry case in sha256_file to `preview: unreadable
  <path>`, exit 2, no traceback, and a bash scan refuses a dangling entry
  under docs/ before any preview write.

Brief vs tests: no difference. The tests are the source of truth for the
pinned texts and were followed. The F3 line follows the brief default and
is stated in the preview.sh header.

